From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:56:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Cap: require the exact Lean release at both ends of
 execution and re-check sources

gate.py --execute now requires the last line of `lake env lean --version` to
fully match the pinned version, its official release commit
(5045d0056413266e57c625dcd7c365b10e377c52) and a Release build, with only
`info:` lines allowed before it. The runtime, the dependency checkouts and the
bound source identity are observed before the first and after the last Lean
execution and must agree. The receipt records both observations under
`observations`. Every existing receipt key is unchanged.

Scientific effect: NONE. No Lean was run for this change. It changes no Lean
statement and establishes nothing about one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
